---
/**
 * The frame the shelter-facing pages share.
 *
 * Deliberately thin — a document, a heading and a slot. It exists because six pages landed
 * at once with issue #51 and the alternative was six copies of the same `<head>`, not
 * because a design system is being started here.
 *
 * **No stylesheet and no script.** Both are real decisions rather than things not done yet:
 * ADR 0007's rule is that the Worker runs as rarely as possible and the payload is small on
 * a metered Venezuelan connection, and every page in this group is a form that has to work
 * before any of that arrives. The look belongs to the ticket that designs the publishing
 * area; what these pages owe the shelter is that the words are right and the form submits.
 *
 * The copy is es-VE, hard-coded, matching `index.astro` and `a/[id]/[...name].astro`. ADR 0018
 * settles that UI strings become typed phrase functions in a `strings/` workspace; that
 * workspace does not exist yet and standing it up needs a per-locale routing decision
 * Astro does not make for us, which belongs with the listing (#56/#57) rather than with
 * auth. `CONTEXT.md`'s *User-facing Spanish* table governs the words used here.
 */
interface Props {
  title: string;
  heading: string;
}

const { title, heading } = Astro.props;
---

<html lang="es">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title} — Pawster</title>
    <!--
      Never indexed. Every page in this group is either a credential form or a shelter's own
      publishing area, and a search engine holding a cached copy of one is all cost and no
      benefit — nobody arrives at a sign-in form through search.
    -->
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>{heading}</h1>
    <slot />
  </body>
</html>
